# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Every route is prerendered to its own HTML file, so publishing a post changes
# the HTML for several URLs at once. Those must revalidate, or the edge serves
# yesterday's page from the custom domain until someone purges the cache by hand.
#
# Rules are matched on the request path, not the file on disk — /blog/a-post has
# no .html extension even though it serves blog/a-post/index.html — so the
# default below is deliberately everything, with the fingerprinted build assets
# opted back out underneath it.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Vite fingerprints these (index-D8YDSLiX.js), so the name changes whenever the
# contents do and they can be held indefinitely.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
